# Question hierarchy (bootloader — spec in `docs/modules/question-hierarchy.md`, ADR-009)

## Invariants
- Tree via `questions.parent_id` (`ON DELETE RESTRICT`). `part` is the **own** label (`a`, `i`); `qno` is the integer start; `qno_end` marks a range stem (`Q23-24`). Range and part-path are mutually exclusive.
- QNO grammar lives in `app/hierarchy.py` (`QNO_TOKEN_PATTERN`, `parse_qno_token`, `parse_qid`, `ensure_question`). Do not add another `Q\\d+` regex.
- `QuestionAsset.part_number` is IMG page N of one QID. Filename `..._QUE_2.png` ≠ sub-question `..._Q3a_QUE.png`.
- `ensure_question` is the only create path that must understand parents (ingest, Smart Import, admin create, Split commit, PDF commit).
- `QuestionAsset.asset_type=WHOLE` is IMG-only on a **root** (`Q5`, not `Q5a` / `Q23-24`). Dashboard, generator, viewer, Explain, auto-tag never read it. Combine **restore** copies WHOLE→QUE; nested stems always **reconstruct**.
- Sort by `hierarchy.sort_key` / `qno_sort_key`, not natsort of the QID string (`Q3ci` vs `Q3civ`).
- Delete stem blocked while children exist unless `delete_children`. Sync never drops a childless-asset row that still has children.
- Generator/viewer expansion is **only** `resolve_render_plan` (`hierarchy_mode` `selected`|`whole`). Dashboard selection (`selectedQuestions`, `#allQuestionIds`) stays **leaves only**; stem / substem checkboxes are aggregates over `data-leaf-ids`, never stored ids. Anything that shows a part's background (viewer `context`, Explain, docx) must go through `resolve_render_plan([leaf])` / `ancestors` + `earlier_siblings`, never just the root. Selection semantics stay ADR-008.
- Tags live on leaves. Do not write topic/type/level onto stems. Auto-tag skips stems.
- PDF import: pass 1 = whole numbered questions; pass 2 (`iter_split_detect`) = stem+(a)(b)(c), nested as plain labels (`4d` + `4di`). `Subject.split_parts_default` seeds the wizard checkbox.
- Plan roles are **derived** (`derive_roles` / `label_is_ancestor`), never stored from model output. A nested stem is just a node with children.
- `needs_prev_parts` is the only sibling-dependency mechanism: `resolve_render_plan` prepends `earlier_siblings` as `stem`-role items for flagged leaves (selected mode). No `depends_on` edges (ADR-009/010).

## Gotchas
- Hyphen in Smart Import: match qno on the **unsplit** stem (`Q23-24`), not `_SPLIT_RE` tokens.
- Empty parent rows from `..._Q3a` ingest are load-bearing; do not "clean them up" in sync. Health no-assets / untagged lists skip them.
- Do not create children by only setting `parent_id` on a full-question image — the stem QUE must be the background only (Split tool / PDF pass 2).
- Split commit calls `replace_img_assets` per version (each call commits). Partial crops are possible if a later version fails. On a root, commit copies the staged PNG to WHOLE **before** cropping when that slot is empty.
- Combine loads all subtree IMG pages into memory, writes the survivor, then deletes descendants. Do not delete children first. Range stems return 409. Bulk selection collapses to maximal stems (`collapse_maximal_stems`).
- Pass-2 crop mapping uses unpadded crops then `full_width_child_box` (parent x1/x2 kept). Auto-tag / MD QUE / Explain prepend ancestor QUE; proofread does not.
